   "daf": "122a",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "וְהָלְכוּ וְלֹא מָצְאוּ. וְדִלְמָא שֵׁד הֲוָה? אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר רַב: שֶׁרָאוּ לוֹ דְּמוּת אָדָם. אִינְהוּ נָמֵי דָּמוּ! דַּחֲזוֹ לֵיהּ בָּבוּאָה.",
   "en": "With regard to the incident where «they» heard a disembodied voice but «went and found no» person there, which is mentioned in the mishna, the Gemara asks: «Perhaps it was a demon. Rav Yehuda said» that «Rav said: They saw that he had the form of a person,» so they knew it was not a demon. The Gemara asks: «They,» i.e., demons, «also appear similar» to people. The Gemara answers: «They saw that he had a shadow.»"
  }
 ],
